"""
## Purpose and audience
This unit spec covers the pure-Simple web renderer path used by browser, web,
and Engine2D-backed GUI surfaces. It checks HTML-to-scene conversion,
HTML-to-pixel rendering, selector cascade behavior, text raster behavior,
Chrome-parity matrix fixtures, static pixel caching, backend-name resolution,
and corpus fixture rendering. Audience: engineers changing the web renderer
pipeline and reviewers of its Chrome-parity evidence.

The Draw IR Phase 4 scenario verifies the semantic inspection side of the same
layout pipeline: `simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir` emits an `html_ast`
Draw IR batch with computed style and border/content/hit/clip rectangles before
the pixel renderer paints the page.

## Operator workflow
Run this file with the Simple test runner from the repository root
(`simple run test/01_unit/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_renderer_spec.spl`).
Scenarios feed real HTML through `simple_web_render_html_to_scene`,
`simple_web_render_html_to_pixels`, and the Draw IR inspector, then pin scene
shapes, pixel bytes, and computed-style entries.

## Compatibility and limitations
These scenarios are implementation and architecture evidence for the Simple Web
renderer and the active Draw IR inspection plan rather than numbered product
requirements. Several Chrome-parity scenarios are legitimately RED at baseline
(background shorthand, backdrop grammar, WM material projection) and stay RED
until the pipeline implements those primitives — do not weaken them.

## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A failure names the scenario's HTML fixture and the scene or pixel property
that diverged; replay the fixture through the render entry points before
changing the renderer. Pixel assertions remain the rendering oracle; Draw IR
assertions inspect semantic layout metadata before raster, so a Draw IR miss
with green pixels points at the inspector, not the painter.

**Lifecycle plan:** doc/03_plan/ui/draw_ir/draw_io_sdn_draw_ir_plan.md
**Lifecycle architecture:** doc/04_architecture/ui/simple_gui_stack.md
**Lifecycle research:** doc/01_research/ui/draw_ir/draw_io_sdn_draw_ir.md
**Lifecycle design:** doc/05_design/ui/gpu_web_scene_contracts.md

## Syntax

The spec uses `std.spec` scenarios and the built-in matcher vocabulary. Pixel
assertions remain the rendering oracle; Draw IR assertions inspect semantic
layout metadata before raster.
"""
# @manual_section: simple web renderer

